    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n16265" root="رفى" body-key="r">
    
      <b><span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">أُرْفِىٌّ</span></b>  <i>Pure milk:</i> (IAar, TA:) or <i>milk of a
gazelle:</i> or <i>pure and good milk:</i> (M, K:) ISd
says, it may be of the measure <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">أُفْعُولٌ</span>, or <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">فُعْلِىٌّ</span>;
or it may belong to art. <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">رفو</span>, because one says
<span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">رَفَوْتُ</span>, but not [to his knowledge] <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">رَفَيْتُ</span>. (TA.)

